# ============================================================================
# GWIscan family table — SUPERFAMILY mode (families grouped under a superfamily)
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file to  config/superfamily.tsv  and edit it for your study families,
# and set  MODE: superfamily  in config.yaml.
#
# Superfamily mode adds a superfamily rollup on top of the per-family results
# (e.g. Lectin over GNA, Legume, CRA). Every processing step matches family mode;
# the leading Superfamily column drives the rollup.
#
# One row per family. TAB-separated. Whole-line '#' comments and blank lines are
# ignored (put each comment on its own line beginning with '#').
#
# COLUMNS  (family-mode columns, with a leading Superfamily column)
#   Superfamily The grouping label this family rolls up into. Required in this
#               mode; families sharing a value are reported together.
#
#   Family      Study family name. Used verbatim in outputs and domain ids
#               (e.g. GNA -> AthGNA001.1). Required and unique.
#
#   PfamModel   How the family is identified and confirmed — one of:
#                 PFxxxxx   Pfam accession: hmmscan + DIAMOND, then confirmed by
#                           InterProScan reporting that Pfam. Use only for a Pfam
#                           specific to the family.
#                 name.hmm  custom family-specific HMM in db/hmm/: hmmscan (this
#                           HMM) + DIAMOND, merged, NO InterProScan; its own
#                           hmmscan hit gives the coordinates. Its NAME line must
#                           equal the Family. Use when the family's Pfam is a
#                           shared/ancestral domain, not specific to the family.
#                 -         no HMM: DIAMOND only, merged, no InterProScan.
#
#   BlastModel  Reference protein FASTA (in db/blast/) used as the DIAMOND round-1
#               query. DIAMOND runs for every family, so this is required for all.
#
# Rule: InterProScan runs ONLY for families whose PfamModel is a Pfam accession.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Superfamily	Family	PfamModel	BlastModel
# specific Pfam -> hmmscan + DIAMOND, InterProScan-confirmed:
Lectin	GNA	PF01453	AAA33346.1.fasta
Lectin	Legume	PF00139	AAA33983.1.fasta
# custom curated HMM (in db/hmm/CRA.hmm) -> hmmscan + DIAMOND, merged, no InterProScan:
Lectin	CRA	CRA.hmm	ABL98074.1.fasta
# no HMM -> DIAMOND only, merged, no InterProScan:
Lectin	EUL	-	ABW73993.1.fasta
